  "term": "midazolam",
  "definition": "Midazolam is a short-acting benzodiazepine with anxiety-reducing, memory-impairing, sleep-inducing, anticonvulsant, and sedating effects. It works in the central nervous system by acting at the GABA receptor complex to strengthen GABA’s inhibitory effects.",
